// Bug 2.24: @spritecompiler is dead code on every target, not just
// C64. Its handler calls img->SpriteCompiler(...) and appends whatever
// it returns to Parser::m_parserAppendix, but the base LImage::
// SpriteCompiler (the only one reachable on this fork's C64-only image
// classes) is a no-op stub, and m_parserAppendix itself is never read
// by anything else in the compiler even when it does hold real text.
// Compilation succeeds, but nothing about the sprite name ever reaches
// the generated assembly: no new symbol, no data.
// Fix direction chosen: raise a clear compile error instead of silently
// producing no output (same resolution as 2.15/2.16), rather than
// implementing real sprite-compiler output wiring as new feature work.
// Method B (compile-time only): pre-fix this compiles clean (COMPILE_OK,
// FAIL per the harness's inverted expectation for this batch); post-fix
// it must fail to compile (COMPILE_ERROR, PASS).
program Bug_2_24_SpriteCompilerDeadCode;

@spritecompiler "sample_sprite.flf" "bug224sprite" 0 0 8 8

begin
	loop();
end.
